                                                                                                                                                                                     HELP                 To display this  DOCUMENTOR  application   This utility expects a documentation disk in Drive 1.           SUMMARY              Displays all words in the file.            /VOCABULARY _____    Displays all words in vocabulary _____ .   VOCAB _____          Specifies vocabulary for entries & searchesn SOURCE !           Specifies source block  n  for entries.    ENTER _____          Enters  ____  making it current.              Thereafter use  U  to enter descriptive text.                FIND _____           Locates and shows _____ making it current. F                    Re-displays the current word.              n AT                 Changes the current word's source to  n .  STACKS               Enter 'input' and 'output' stack arguments.l T  ( or  t)        Types line  l (0-n)  making it current.    P  ( or  p ) _____   Puts  _____  on the current line.          U  ( or  u ) _____   Inserts  _____  under the current line.    The date used for today's entries will be                       ( Documentor utility)      FORGET TASK   : TASK ;  40 ALLOT     : HELP   140 DATED ;   HELP   ( File)  142 LOAD                 : (SHOW)   FIRST  NAME ?B  VOC ?B  BEFORE ?B  AFTER ?B             SOURCE ?N  ENTERED N@  .M/D/Y  BEGIN +L  -NEXT NOT WHILE           10 SPACES  PHRASE B?  REPEAT ;                            : GLOSS ( n)   (GLOSSARY) READ  LINK N@ DUP 0 > IF  HEAD !         GLOSSARY FIRST 1  ELSE DROP 0  THEN ;                        [R FORTH, INC GLOSSARY\ NAME         VOCABULARY   INPUT            OUTPUT           BLK      ENTERED]   CONSTANT TITLE          VARIABLE #L   ( Data entry)  143 LOAD                           : ?LINES   1 BEGIN 1+  -NEXT UNTIL  ?PAGE ;                     : SUMMARY   TITLE LAYOUT  (GLOSSARY) RECORDS DO  I GLOSS IF        ?LINES  (SHOW)  THEN LOO