                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            System done recently:                                           * Understand failsafe, maint override states.                   * Make PROMs that work                                          * Get enough RAM to target, verify reproduction                 * Figure out why we have trouble resynching on restart          * Determine whether restart thru RAM is safe                    * Test and identify interrupts, check edge/level sensing        * Get interrupting clock working                                * Measure basal performance examples                            * Finish documenting their I/O addresses and interrupt options  * Work out strategem for characterizing boards                  * Start making characterizations and critiques                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  EXP done recently:                                              DACU.0 4/25/88  DACU.X0 4/25/88                                 * Normalize nucleus with MRC.0 source base.                     EXP.5 vEXP.3  1/05/88                                             CUT NEW PROMs with fixes for modem initialization in nuc!     EXP.3 vEXP.1  11/06/87  -- 4-CHIP MEM, NEEDS A16 KLUDGE --      * Move RAM org up to 16k, get working on single mem board.      EXP.2  10/28/87                                                 * Start watchdog on auto fireup.  DOG starts it from debug term.EXP.1  10/15/87                                                 * Preserve sign of saturated A-D in low byte.                   * Invert initial command outputs (472'S ARE NANDS!)             EXP.0                                                           * FIX @PAR BCD BUG (3a has the correction).                     * Explicit test for 000 and FFF; return 7Fxx as saturation flag.* Failsafe relay management                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Recent RT:                                                      RT.1XF 10/03/88                                                 * Slope/intercept cal if feasible                               * PC backup/restore protocol                                    * EAROM overflow diagnostics (FPAN, CRT, LOG)                   * EAROM enlargement (switches)                                  * Logger channel names on alarms                                * Logger date at top of page                                    RT.0 6/09/88                                                    * Default control failsafe & such timeouts on fresh data base.  * Limit CRT duty cycle when controlling a telem channel.        RT.0XC 6/06/88                                                  * Change "---" to "-UNDEF" in HELP lists.                       * CRT option; CRT nomenclature on FPAN.                         * BUG; control failsafe alarm not filed if any configured modem     is not powered up or connected.                             Older RT:                                                       RT.0XB 5/02/88                                                  * Dialup phone no. setups                                       * Dialup on alarm when time criterion met.                      * Remember maint mode in RT across power failures.              * Alarm display for CT control requests (mastership page)       * Data base & FPAN edits for Ft0,1,2; security code.            * Mastership request/grant protocols, decision making.          * Whoever acknowledges control failsafe warning becomes master. * Control failsafe timers, relay, alarms, display, management.                                                                  MRC.0 4/25/88  RT.0XA 4/28/88                                   * ID handshake incoming/outgoing calls.                         * Dialup line management (answering, hangup, line timeouts)     * Short structures, other nucleus savings.                      * Editor out of nuc, replaced by CT/RT common.                  Yet older RT:                                                   RT.H 3/18/88                                                    * Event queue entry & management.                               * Protocols for CT logger option.                               RT.G 2/22/88                                                    * Accept ACK, Status clear only from master                     * Clock/calendar maint from network.                            * Protocol 0CD for CT setting limits.                           * Reassign 488 & config alarms from 1,2 to 6,7.                 * Alarm @ 1min into telem FS, expiration of telem FS.           RT.F 2/19/88                                                    * SETUP LED missing on command, status setups                   * Async rqsts C8-CC inclusive (cmd id's thru rqst limits)       RT.E 2/16/88                                                    * File memory -30v power supply turnoff delay.                  * Protocol for requesting command ID's.                         Recent CT:                                                      CT.1XF 10/03/88                                                 * EAROM overflow diagnostics (FPAN, CRT, LOG)                   * EAROM enlargement (switches)                                  * Logger channel names on alarms                                * Logger date at top of page                                    * COMM LINE SETUP? delete question mark                                                                                         CT.0XC 6/05/88  aka CT.0 6/09/88                                * Internal alarms:  A/B comm; A/B dial fail; A/B dial sever     * Internal alarms to logger queues.                             * A/B labeling on CRT comm %ages.                               * FPAN running displays to show chan & status names.            * Positive generation of "?" on data when ANYONE takes control. * FPAN page to allow/prevent TAKE CONTROL by any CRT's.                                                                         Older CT:                                                       CT.0XB 5/02/88                                                  * Show data link quality %ages on normal CRT screens.           * Align status to right on printer.                             * Incoming calls                                                * Back door password from FPAN S2|S1 as per cheat sheet given.  * "F" Button for telem fs's obtain & display on CRT.            * Password on Restricted entry (CRT)                            * CRT keys ^d and ^k for dialup                                 * CRT, FPAN multi master support.  Annunc master on 0 FPAN page.* Control failsafe alarms handled FPAN, CRT, Logger.            * BUG:  CT CRASHES when calling an RT with bad seculrity code?! * Assert restricted CRT commands not worth their cost.          * Assert password on LIMITS button at CT FPAN not worth its cost* Assert 1-rel MDC button numbering inconsistent, won't do it.  * Assert logger "X" and "C" obsolete.                           Yet older CT:                                                   MRC.0 4/25/88  CT.0XA 4/28/88                                   * Enable ID handshake                                           * Short structures, other nucleus savings.                      * BUG:  Hangs if absent line configured as Dialup!!             * BUG:  Modem reset nukes adjacent channel.                     * Manual dialing, hangup                                        * Editor out of nuc, replaced by CT/RT common.                  * Basic dialup capabilities & setup screens.                                                                                    CT.8 4/18/88                                                    * 3/14 4-sec command timeout on cmd/sts vs telem.  (7E 3/29/88) * Rename COM-STS as SYSTEM on CRT.  (7E)                        * 3/14 Cut normal command timeout to 20 sec.  (7E)              * Send CRT's to page 1 if it exists on powerup.  (7E)           * BUG:  FPAN LED mismanagement with multiple sites.  ( 7E)      dF  returns value that should be in FPD and "true" if it's chgd.-FP  nukes the values in fALM, fDATA demanding fresh data.      ?FC  is used if we might have changed our selected channel or      data family.  Site change must -FP directly.                                                                                 >OP  establishes the front panel in the OPERATE mode, and stores   a code into #CHAN 2+:  0=system pages, 1=telem, 2=status,       3=command.  This code is used to facilitate interpretation of   #CHAN itself when executing functions common to multiple data   page families.                                               >SET  establishes the front panel in SETUP mode for current fam.                                                                -rl  turns off the raise/lower LED's.                           ?CM  is true if we are sitting on a control page at present.    -CM  gets us out of a control page if we are looking at one.                                                                    >OP  establishes the front panel in the OPERATE mode, and stores   a code into #CHAN 2+:  0=system pages, 1=telem, 2=status,       3=command.  This code is used to facilitate interpretation of   #CHAN itself when executing functions common to multiple data   page families.                                               >SET  establishes the front panel in SETUP mode for current fam.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                NIL  enables a nonprinting field that may be used for channel or   page entry.  When used with ENTER we can stay within the        current page or advance to the next one.                                                                                     GHOST  enables a 3-digit field that appears only when active.                                                                   NNN  is display/edit behavior for a basic garden variety 3-digit   numeric field.                                               <eng>  is display/edit behavior for garden variety engrg values.<lim>  is used only for limits with trailing trouble star.      <bit>  is used for yes/no options with numeric keyin option.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    ~lm  toggles the state of the limit enable flag  ?LIM ,  making    the LIMITS led track its state.                              ~Lms  additionally ACKNOWLEDGES ALL ALARMS.  Note that this does   not file any acknowledgement events, but it DOES make the       horn shut up.  ALL alarms are so dealt with, including at the   moment all system alarms.                                                                                                    ?CM  is true if FPAN is in CONTROL MODE.                                                                                        ~Maint  toggles the state of maintenance mode flag  ?MNT , and     makes both the MAINT led and the MAINT relay track its state.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                /ALM  decodes an alarm number, returning channel number in oper-   ator units, class as FP page no. (2=telem, 3=status, all rest   system alarms), and original alarm number.                                                                                   ?ACK  finds the LOWEST NUMBERED alarm (sys, status, telem) that    still needs acknowledgement.  The alarm is acknowledged and     the relevant front panel display page is selected.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           ?loc  shared with CRT; given RT#, returns alarm no. under True     if any of its local CT alarms is active or needs ack.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        FPC  given front panel command (12 raise, 8 lower, 0 lift) sets    command action for this channel using that mode.  Splits back   out of control pages if unable to latch onto it.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             .TLM  types value of current channel in current field.          (STS)  takes engineering value for a status or command channel     and returns addr count for typing.                           <b>  given engineering value, types latest value of sts or cmd     channel iff it has changed from last time we output it.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      lst  returns critical line status flags in engineering format:     cccccccc.0000Mlma slo  - comm alrm, Master, alrm, menu, alt                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  DTIN  for special case of data entry key 'ack/clr', checks for     outstanding alarms acknowledgement before passing the key       along to field data input word executed by  FENT .           aKBD  is a table of vectors used by front panel key entry: raw     keycodes are xlated by  KEYS  into a useful byte under          a class no., where class no. selects which of these three       vectors is executed.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         -PW  true if given password is no good.  Includes back door that   is computed from hex value of S2|S1 using Greg's standard 16-   bit random generator to challenge the genius of our bad guy.    Presumes that Moseley folks have a cheat sheet or can do good   arithmetic in their heads.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   The CRT LOCK flag inhibits CRT's from taking control or indeed     from taking any further control actions.  If a CRT happens to   have control at the time we set the lockout, we may wait for    as long as 20 seconds before we get control back.  If space     is available later,  2fre @ 1- cTO !  will speed this up        considerably.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                th  converts a slot number relative to the current (TH) CRT to     a system wide C.xxx table index.                                                                                             chn  dismantles a channel descriptor, returning channel within     class under class number (0=cmd, 1=sts, 2=tlm).              Chn  adds separate decodes 3=blank 4=text)                                                                                      Fetch  takes channel#, returns actual current value in eng form.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                ~menu  dismantles a menu item number in stored Menu form to be     compatible with the  C.MENU  table in  V!  order , defaulting   current site for site-0 items.                                                                                               -CRT  marks the given system wide CRT slot as having no value.                                                                  M~  nondestructively compares a new and old menu item, disregard   ing the site number field of the channel descriptor.         !MENU  sets a given menu item in the given slot for the current    CRT.                                                                                                                         ~MENU  refreshes active menus for potentially new default site. ~SIT  is for use ONLY in page zero; switches between default and   site specific channel ID's.  This is so we can explicitly       edit in the two modes without confusion.                                                                                     #FM  points to the current item in EAROM.                       E.top  contains the address past the top of EAROM.              E.bot  is address of the -1'th item in this system.                                                                             ?MORE  advances to the next slot in EAROM, returning args set up   for reading 3 bytes from that address unless we have reached    end of file, in which case caller is exited.  Skips over the    RT's main configuration board.                                                                                               Masked  given 3-byte target and mask, aligned in high orders,      underneath 3 bytes from ROM, compares target and ROM under      the mask.  Returns all args and true if match passes; other-    wise discards ROM data and returns false.                                                                                                                                                                                                                    Zero  rewinds the "file".                                       ZIP  blasts forward with a masked search, returning true if a      match is found before end of file.                           EXACT  is true if an exact masked match can be found.  Leaves      FR# positioned for the item.                                 Slot  is true (addr) if an empty item can be found.  Sets PB for   any out of room condition since PB last zeroed.              Scratch  wipes out the current item.                                                                                            ?two  given item number, qual nibble, and kind byte, composes      a 2-byte search value; places it in PAD; and searches for the   item, returning "true" if found.                             ?2f  returns the given item in PAD if it was found.             ?2s  stores the item in PAD in the data base, creating a new       item if it didn't already exist.                             ?2-  deletes the given item from the data base if it existed.   <CP  finds the three possible items for a given CRT page, re-      turning true if the full menu could be found.                                                                                -CP  deletes the current CRT page.                                                                                              +PH  tries to guarantee that the current page has a heading item   allocated.  Returns its ROM address, zero if unable.            Also returns with the item itself in PAD .                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   ?Cid  is true if the record at the given address has an exact      match for three full bytes.                                  -Cid  scratches a record matching that at the given address.    !Cid  is a search and replace for the given record, returning      true if successful.  These words may be used for channel ID's   (record type 10) and comment lines (type 11).                                                                                +CI  tries to guarantee that the currently selected item has an    ID record allocated of either channel or comment line types.    Returns its ROM address, zero if unable; the item is in PAD.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 <IDS  fills the C.ID table for the current CRT with EAROM addr's   for all items in the menu having descriptions in the data       base.  Access to EAROM is so slow that we must expend the       energy to do this in one pass.                                                                                               SATISFIED  is an internal subroutine that matches the current      item with any menu entries still needing satisfaction.  Re-     turns "true" if the entire menu has been satisfied.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          IS  types the given tagged attribute byte.                      att  makes Normal, Low Int, Inverse, Inv/Blink, Invisible.                                                                      DEFAULT:  1B 54 Local Mode/Online; 1B 42 Remove status line;       1B 06 Keyboard Unlock; 17 Cursor Off                                                                                         pos  returns screen coordinates for the given menu item.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        LJ  formats a number in a left justified field.                 .S#  refreshes the site number field.                                                                                           .D/T  shows current date and time if changed.                                                                                   -R/L  defaults the raise/lower effects fields.                                                                                  .ann  displays the annunciator zone and sets its "last" data.                                                                   .SU  displays SETUP line.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       .PG  displays the static portions of a page skeleton.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           .id  formats a command action given command mode/1-rel channel     and "raise" action flag.  Channel 0 means nothing is assigned   For all other channels, all commands mean "ON" state except     in the case of "lower" with a latched command.  If nomenclat-   ure exists in the data base for the channel in question, we     use the existing channel name; otherwise we synthesize one.     If named on/off states exist we use them; otherwise faked.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   .id  formats a standard channel description code ssKnnn .       .ID  refreshes the identity of the given slot number.           -ID  blanks the given slot, perhaps useful when updating.                                                                       .BODY  refreshes all slot identifications.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      [sts]  formats commands and status with user nomenclature if       such have been provided.  ON-state is the one that's edited     in the data column at user interface.                                                                                        SHOW  updates a single slot.                                                                                                    CHGD  puts up value of all channels that have actually changed.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ?SL  is true if there is a channel selected at present.         ->S  positions to selected field.                               -SL  deselects the currently selected channel, if any.  Raise/     lower command annunciators are cleared back to default.      .SEL  highlights the currently selected channel, if any.                                                                        ~SL  MUST BE USED BEFORE DEPENDING ON RT# CONSISTENCY WITH THE     SELECTED CHANNEL!                                            SCH  returns channel and class for current selection.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           WHAT  is current or previous selected channel ID.               WHOM  is the RT involved; these valid iff WHERE positive.       WHERE  is the slot number (-1 if none) to be updated.  If this     differs from #CHAN, we don't update & we don't allow raise/     lower either.                                                                                                                >RL  sets raise/lower annunciators given command function code.                                                                 ?KM  is true if the CRT is currently set for command mode.      -TC  withdraws from command mode.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ?an  returns annunciator data for current RT# in V@ format:        ---- --SR Cuas Mmla  Sys-alm,Restricted                            Comm-alm,menu,alt,slo Master,maint,lims,alm                                                                               ANTS  is a table of annunciator attributes working upward from     low order in the bitmask returned by  ?ann .                                                                                 .ANN  refreshes annunciators if they have changed.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              .Fld  updates the ghost editing field at top of screen.         KLEAR  wipes this field.                                                                                                        HYPH  is vectored to when user types minus.                     !DIG  is vectored to when user types a digit.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   LEGAL  given channel and class numbers returns legal menu item. GEN  generates a synthetic menu given a starting channel no.       and class number in  chn  notation.  The menu produced will     start on a mod-32 boundary.                                                                                                  ~ID  refreshes the selected row of the display.                 -TXT  kills the selected row's descriptive text.                                                                                .PAGE  prints the entire current page.                          !PAGE  ensures that a good menu exists for the current nonzero     page, creating it if nonexistent and updating it from C.MENU.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <KEYS>  is interrupt code for incoming characters from the         optional crt. If the character is an xoff, we set  FLG  and     disable the output interrupt. If we are already xoff'd, then    any non-xoff character is considered an xon, and we clear       the xoff flag, and enable the output interrupt iff we were      typing.  Function key sequences {stx|x|cr) are recognized;      the central character {x} is made unique by turning on its      sign bit and is returned that way.  All other characters in     the lower case range are converted to upper case.  Incoming     characters are inserted in the ring buffer  keys  and the       appropriate CRT task is awakened through its  WHIP .                                                                         NOTE!  This mapping makes space bar equivalent to ACK/CLR!      2/14:  Lower case converted to upper.                                                                                                                                                           ?ED  is true if we're in setup mode and a slot is selected.                                                                     !M  places the given value in the currently selected page's menu   updating EAROM and CRT as necessary.  If the menu item was      previously a -2 (comment), we delete its text (if any).                                                                      ?del  given length and PAD offset of the given item, scratches     it and returns zero if the said field is all blank.          PIN  prompts input, updating the indicated field in PAD if there   was anything typed.  Turns cursor on at start, off at end.      MUST RESET INTERRUPT ROUTINE after finished with a series!                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Rest  toggles restricted func enable.  NEEDS PASSWORDS!         !RF  exits the caller if restricted funcs are not enabled.                                                                      !sel  picks given slot number, turning previously selected         slot back to low intensity if one was selected.              sel  given delta, selects a channel: same, next, or previous.   Cr  reacts to carriage return by selecting first, next, or         previous channel on screen.                                  CTRL  produces evidence of taking control by showing selected      channel in inverse video.                                    -L'S  toggles state of limit checking.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          +-n  increments the argument if nothing entered, decrements it     if "-" entered, or returns specific number if one entered.      Decrementation may not go below one.                                                                                         Unq  toggles between generic and unique channel ID's if we are     looking at one of the vanilla channel display pages.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ^r  rude request for control from current site (RESTRICTED)     ^p  polite request (RESTRICTED)                                 ^y  grant request for control                                   ^n  deny same                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   /ALM  decodes an alarm number, returning channel number in oper-   ator units, class as FP page no. (2=telem, 3=status, all rest   system alarms), and original alarm number.                                                                                   ?ACK  finds the LOWEST NUMBERED alarm (sys, status, telem) that    still needs acknowledgement.  The alarm is acknowledged and     the relevant front panel display page is selected.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           ^W  requires that we be in setup mode with a selection made; and   if we're looking at page 0 we must be looking at actual chans   Straight blank lines are marked as headings.                                                                                 ^E  enters a page title, editing if already existent, creating     if not there, and finally deleting if all blank.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             THINGS  is a table of vectors for reacting to crt keypresses.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   KEES  takes a keystroke and returns position in table where it     was found; returns max ( #K'S ) for all digits 0-9; if          keystroke makes NO sense, bumps I past next word in caller.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  <key  returns false if no new key is available, or true over      keystroke from circular buffer.                               ?INKEY  for as many keys are in input buffer (max 8), vectors     through  THINGS .                                             CYCLING  is  TUBE 's runtime behavior.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          ‡a‡=‡a‡␀‡aˇˇ‡a␀‡a␀‡a␀‡a␀‡a␀‡a␀
